{"id":"word:hebrew:H216","type":"word","title":"אוֹר","subtitle":"H216 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"illumination or (concrete) luminary (in every sense, including lightning, happiness, etc.)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אוֹר (H216) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 121 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אוֹר (ʼôwr) means illumination or (concrete) luminary (in every sense, including lightning, happiness, etc.) First listed occurrence: 1Sam 14 36."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אוֹר","transliteration":"ʼôwr","pronunciation":"ore","strong":"H216","lemmaId":"hebrew:H216","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["אֽוֹר","א֑וֹר","א֣וֹר","א֥וֹר","לְ/א֣וֹר"],"morphs":[["HNcbsa",40],["HR/Ncbsc",16],["HNcbsc",12],["HRd/Ncbsa",10],["HR/Ncbsa",8],["HTd/Ncbsa",7],["HNcbsc/Sp3ms",5],["HC/Ncbsc",5],["HC/Ncbsa",3],["HNcbsc/Sp3mp",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"illumination or (concrete) luminary (in every sense, including lightning, happiness, etc.)","usage":"bright, clear, day, light (-ning), morning, sun.","full":"H216. or אוֺר 121 noun masculine Gen 1:3 ( feminine Job 36:32 ; Jer 13:16 ) light (Assyrian urru = ûru Dl w ). — absolute Gen 1:3 +; construct Judg 16:2 +; suffix אוֺרִי Psa 27:1 , etc.; plural אוֺרִים 136:7 ; &#8212; 1 light as diffused in nature, light of day Gen 1:3-4 , 5 (P) Job 3:9 ; 38:19 +. 2 morning light, dawn , הַבֹּקֶר אוֺר light of the morning Judg 16:2 ; 1Sam 14:36 ; 25:34 , 36 ; 2Sam 17:22 ; 2Kin 7:9 ; Micah 2:1 ; ׳א בֹּקֶר 2Sam 23:4 (poem of David); ׳עַדהָֿא Judg 19:26 (compare עַדהַֿבֹּקֶר 19:25 ); לָאוֺר Job 24:14 ; הַיּוֺם מַחֲצִית עַד מִןהָֿאוֺר from dawn till mid-day , Neh 8:3 compare Prov 4:18 . 3 light of the heavenly luminaries; ׳א הַלְּבָנָה , || ׳א הַחַמָּה moonlight & sunlight Isa 30:26 ; אוֺר כּוֺכְבֵי stars of light Psa 148:3 ; אוֺר מְאוֺרֵי luminaries of light Ezek 32:8 ; אוֺרִים = מְאוֺרִים Psa 136:7 ; so עֲלֵיאֿוֺר in sunshine Isa 18:4 ; the sun itself Job 31:26 . 4 daylight רְשָׁעִים אוֺר light of the wicked Job 38:15 (their work-day being the night); אוֺר יוֺם a day of light Amos 8:9 (= a clear, sunshiny day). 5 lightning Job 36:32 ; 37:3 , 11 , 15 compare Hab 3:11 . 6 light of lamp Prov 13:9 ; Jer 25:10 ; of crocodile's hot breath Job 41:10 . 7 light of life ׳א חַיִּים Job 33:30 ; Psalm 56:14; compare אוֺר 3:16 , 20 . 8 light of prosperity Job 22:28 ; 30:26 ; Psa 97:11 ; Lam 3:2 . 9 light of instruction אוֺר וְתוֺרָה מִצְוָה נֵר Prov 6:23 the commandment is a lamp and instruction a light ; so the Messian. servant is גּוֺיִם אוֺר Isa 42:6 ; 49:6 ; compare ׳א עַמִּים 51:4 ; the advent of Messiah is shining of great light 9:1 (twice in verse). 10 light of face מָּנִים אוֺר = bright, cheerful face (of men) Job 29:24 ; betokening king's favour Prov 16:15 (compare ׳א עֵינַיִם Psa 38:11 ); of God = his shining, enlightening, favouring face 4:7 ; 44:4 ; 89:16 . 11 Yahweh is ׳א יִשְׂרָאֵל Isa 10:17 , as source enlightenment & prosperity; light & salvation Psa 27:1 ; light to guide Micah 7:8 compare Psa 43:3 ; everlasting light of Zion, instead of sun & moon Isa 60:19-20 , house of Jacob is to walk in his light 2:5 .","rootNote":"from 215 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Sam 14 36","keyReferences":["1Sam 14 36","1Sam 25 34","1Sam 25 36","2Kgs 7 9","2Sam 17 22","2Sam 23 4","Amos 5 18","Amos 5 20"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":121,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Sam 14 36","book":"1Sam","chapter":14,"verse":36,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"א֣וֹר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcbsc"},{"reference":"1Sam 25 34","book":"1Sam","chapter":25,"verse":34,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"א֥וֹר","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcbsc"},{"reference":"1Sam 25 36","book":"1Sam","chapter":25,"verse":36,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"א֥וֹר","source":"hebr